Q1. Count total records
SELECT COOUNT(*)
FROM EMPLOYEES;

Q2. Fetch duplicate records based on EMP_ID
SELECT EMP-ID, COUNT(*)
FROM EMPLOYEE
GROUP BY EMP_ID 
HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;

Q3. Fetch second highest salary
SELECT MAX(SALARY)
FROM EMP
WHERE SALARY < (SELECT MAX(SALARY)
                FROM EMPLOYEE);

Q4. Fetch highest salary
SELECT MAX(SALARY)
FROM EMP;

Q5. Fetch records with salary greater than 40000
SELECT *
FROM EMP
WHERE SALARY > 40000;

Technical round quick revision
1. How do you fetch duplicate records from a DB2 table?
GROUP BY with HAVING COUNT(*) > 1.

2. How do you count records in a sequential file?
Use COBOL READ loop and increment a counter until end-of-file.

3. How do you compare two sequential files?
Use DFSORT JOINKEYS.

4. How do you remove duplicate records from a file?
SORT FIELDS with SUM FIELDS=NONE.

5. How do you fetch records present in file 1 but missing in file 2?
Use JOINKEYS with JOIN UNPAIRED,F1 and filter the indicator for F1-only records.


